The verifier no longer proves false facts about nested bitvector rotations at widths that are not powers of two, such as `x.RotateRight(a).RotateLeft(b) == 4` for `x == 1 as bv3`, `a == 3` and `b == 0`, where the value is 1.  Z3 combined the counts of nested rotations modulo 2^W instead of modulo W.  At positive widths that are not powers of two, `RotateLeft` and `RotateRight` are now verified through a definition by shifts; at width 0 and at powers of two, such as 8, 32 and 64, they keep Z3's native rotations, for which that combination is sound (https://github.com/erniecohen/dafny/issues/147).
